# Cloudflare Pages security headers. CSP allows the inlined stylesheet
# (astro.config `inlineStylesheets: 'always'`) via style-src 'unsafe-inline' and
# the inline theme script and analytics stub. The analytics host is a whole token in
# script-src and connect-src, and script-src lets the stub run: 'unsafe-inline' alone, or
# the stub's own sha256 hash (the analytics gate test checks all of it against config.ts and
# the built stub). With analytics switched off (USE_ANALYTICS = false in src/config.ts), take
# the host out of both; run the gate test by hand to check that it is gone. Widen
# script-src/connect-src only as needed.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://analytics.example.com; connect-src 'self' https://analytics.example.com; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
